          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اخبار (akhbâr) — \"the news (programme)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پدرم هر شب ساعت نه اخبار را تماشا میکند. Pedaram har shab sâ'at-e noh akhbâr râ tamâshâ mikonad. My father watches the news every night at nine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Arabic broken plural of khabar \"a piece of news\". Akhbâr is the news in general or the news programme."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "akhbâr is borrowed from Arabic akhbār (EtymDB), the broken plural of khabar \"news\", which Persian also has."
            }
          ]
        },
